This file lists third-party code reused in openkonnect, as required by
CLEANROOM.md ("Permitted third-party code"): code licensed under MIT, BSD,
ISC or Apache-2.0. Files taken from a project also keep that project's
copyright notice in their header.

The full license text of each source, verbatim and including its
copyright line, lives in LICENSES/<source-id>.txt, where <source-id> is
the lowercase owner-repo slug of the upstream repository (for example
LICENSES/mixelpixx-kicad-mcp-server.txt). That file is added in the same
PR that first reuses code from the source, and stays while any of its code
remains; the LICENSES/ directory is created by the first such PR. Each
entry below names its license file on the "License text:" line.

For Apache-2.0 sources, the upstream NOTICE file's attribution notices are
reproduced verbatim in the entry's "Upstream NOTICE:" block (write "none"
when upstream ships no NOTICE file), and each changed file carries a
"Modified by openkonnect" comment in its header.

No third-party code has been reused so far. Add one entry per source
project, in this form:

  <Project name>
    URL:          <upstream repository URL>
    License:      <MIT | BSD-2-Clause | BSD-3-Clause | ISC | Apache-2.0>
    License text: LICENSES/<source-id>.txt
    Copyright:    <upstream copyright line(s)>
    Upstream NOTICE: (Apache-2.0 sources only)
      <upstream NOTICE attribution notices, verbatim, or: none>
    Files taken:
      <openkonnect path>  <-  <upstream path> @ <upstream commit>

